-- title:
--   Original bounded-variation C1 compact-band localisation supplies full same-path H jump integrability
-- statement:
--   For the actual original bounded-variation Lévy process, original admissible dividend strategy, C1 interior candidate, finite ruin/horizon T and any compact positive interior band, the original stopped H kernel is integrable on the actual original global marked count measure almost surely. The proof extracts explicit Lipschitz and lower-space bounds from the already proved original BV C1 localisation certificate and applies the original no-unexplained-hypothesis H integrability theorem. This supplies the exact source hypothesis usable with the accepted indexed compensated HJB certificate and P3-GRID4.

import Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.ContDiff.Defs
import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Exponential
import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Count
